course: dictionary
lesson: 5614
title: Working out lighthouse from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lighthouse is a tall tower by the sea with a bright light at the top that flashes. Its job is to guide ships at night and warn them of rocks. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «It is like a moth flying across a distant lighthouse: you cannot see the moth, but the light flickers.» Distant tells you the lighthouse is far away, and the light flickers tells you it has a light that goes on and off. Those clues help you picture it before you look it up.
explain: «Spinning ones sweep radio beams past the Earth like a lighthouse.» The word like is a clue. A beam that sweeps round and round is what a lighthouse does, so the sentence is comparing the beams to a lighthouse's light.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does a tower by the sea with a flashing light guide ships at night? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: A lighthouse is a tall tower by the sea with a bright light at the top.
fact: Its light flashes to guide ships at night and warn them of rocks.
fact: Each lighthouse has its own pattern of flashes, so sailors know which one it is.
fact: A lighthouse keeper looked after the light.
fact: «Lighthouse» is a noun, and its plural is «lighthouses».
exercise: «It is like a moth flying across a distant lighthouse: you cannot see the moth, but the light flickers.» What is a lighthouse? | *A tall tower by the sea with a bright light that flashes | A small wooden hut in a garden | A kind of moth that flies in the dark | A ship that sails across the sea at night
exercise: Kai says a lighthouse is a boat. What does a lighthouse really do? | Keeps the fish warm in the water | *Guides ships at night and warns them of rocks | Lights up the stars in the sky | Carries people across the sea
exercise: What is the plural of lighthouse? | *lighthouses | lighthouse's | lighthouser | lightshouses
test: Sailors knew which lighthouse they had reached because each one flashed its own pattern. What do the flashes help sailors do? | Keep warm at sea | Count the fish in the water | *Tell which lighthouse it is | Make music on the boat
test: What does a lighthouse keeper do? | *Looks after the light | Paints pictures of the sea | Swims out to the island | Sails the ship to the rocks
exam: «The lighthouse flashed every 10 seconds, warning ships of the rocks.» What is the lighthouse for? | *To guide ships and warn them of rocks | To cook dinner for the sailors | To hide from the wind | To grow flowers in the garden
